TITLE
Embedded Systems Design and Implementation

CHAPTER
02.cad

ABSTRACT
The Ptolemy project studies modeling, simulation, and design of
concurrent, real-time, embedded systems.  The goal of this work is to
study concepts and techniques for integration with Ptolemy II that can
help developers design and implement embedded, real-time systems.
These include programming language concepts, techniques for
communications and networks, and improving the reusability and
reconfigurability of software for embedded systems.
